                "fallback": "Damien Querbes - Empowering scale-ups to unlock revenue through customer data insights and predictions | Data Science | Analytics | Data Architecture | LinkedIn",
                "text": "Empowering scale-ups to unlock revenue through customer data insights and predictions | Data Science | Analytics | Data Architecture · • I help digital scale-ups unlock revenue by leveraging customer data insights and predictive analytics. With 9 years of experience building data warehouses for growth teams, I provide a 360° view of customers that fuels data-driven decision-making. My expertise spans from key SaaS tools like Segment and DBT to the GCP environment, which I use daily to create robust, scalable data solutions.\n• My journey started in Performance Marketing and CMO roles, where close collaboration with CTOs pushed me to dive into data coding. This unique combination of marketing and technical experience allows me to bridge the gap between growth teams and tech, offering end-to-end implementation of data strategies that truly drive growth.\n• In 2023, with AI on the rise and with plenty of customer prediction use cases in mind, it felt like the right time to expand my skills with the 6 month ML\/AI bootcamp at LeWagon. Along with my GCP data engineer certification passed in 2024, I am now autonomous on all the aspects of ML ops in the cloud. \n• Thus, after establishing data warehouses and pipelines, I’ve launched several advanced ML projects to production such as Marketing Mix Modeling, LTV Prediction for new customers, and Uplift Modeling for promotional actions. One of the most underrated strategies, in my opinion, is LTV Prediction. Few companies optimize their campaigns based on lifetime value, and that represents a massive opportunity.\n• If you haven’t explored LTV-based optimizations yet, I’d love to help you unlock this potential in your business. Let’s work together to build data-driven strategies that lead to long-term success! · Experience: DQS Consulting · Education: EM Lyon · Location: Brussels Region · 500+ connections on LinkedIn. View Damien Querbes’ profile on LinkedIn, a professional community of 1 billion members.",
